BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ILLU 150 CELEBRATION Opening Reception\, Website Launch & Fundrais
 er
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T210000
UID:illu-150-celebration-opening-reception-website-launch-fundraiser@ocadu
 .ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the OCAD U ILLU 150 Celebration kickoff with a rec
 eption\, website launch\, and art sale fundraiser! Celebrating 150 years o
 f Illustration at OCAD U\, this exhibition and art sale features work by 4
 0 Illustration alumni and faculty\, spanning generations of artists\, make
 rs\, and visual storytellers.\n\nExhibition runs October 28–November 9\,
  2026 Gallery Hours: Oct 30 - Nov 9 MCA 225 will be open 12-4pm Monday-Fri
 days. Additional visiting hours and tours available by appointment. Please
  email schang@ocadu.ca to arrange. Join us for the OCAD U ILLU 150 Celebra
 tion kickoff with a reception\, website launch\, and art sale fundraiser! 
 Celebrating 150 years of Illustration at OCAD U\, this exhibition and art 
 sale features work by 40 Illustration alumni and faculty\, spanning genera
 tions of artists\, makers\, and visual storytellers. Exhibiting artists: A
 manda Arlotta\, Ashley Barron\, Barbara Reid\, Blair Drawson\, Brandon Cel
 i\, Chen Cao\, Dan Page\, Dmitry Bondarenko\, Fiona Smyth\, Gillian Iles\,
  Greg Mably\, Hudson Christie\, JC Knaff\, Jenn Woodall\, Jinke Wang\, Jod
 y Hewgill\, Jon Todd\, Julia Mathew\, Kathryn Adams\, Kevin Bae\, Kestin C
 ornwall\, Kima Lenaghan\, Kyle Stewart\, Lauchie Reid\, Marc O'Brien (AKA 
 Doras)\, Mathieu Larone\, Misbah Ahmed\, Moya Garrison-Msingwana (Gangbox)
 \, Nicholas Di Genova\, Paul Dallas\, Robert Akow\, Rosena Fung\, Shea Cha
 ng\, Shevon Lewis\, Suharu Ogawa\, Terry Shoffner\, Theo Dimson\, Thomas S
 evalrud\, Tiffany Chin (TWKCHIN)\, Toko Hara. Two special highlights of th
 e celebration will be the exclusive release of a limited-edition Paul Dall
 as print\, created to commemorate ILLU 150 and OCAD University's 150th ann
 iversary\, and the launch of ILLU150.com\, a new digital archive and lookb
 ook documenting the people\, practices\, and history of Illustration at OC
 AD U. Original art for sale by renowned Illustration alumni and faculty of
 fers a unique opportunity to collect work by artists who have helped shape
  the program and the broader field of illustration. Proceeds from artwork 
 sales will support the Illustration Program Initiative Fund\, helping fund
  student opportunities including exhibitions\, industry award entries\, wo
 rkshops\, and extracurricular programming. Join us as we mark this incredi
 ble milestone\, bring our Illustration community together\, and help suppo
 rt the next generation of OCAD U illustrators! This event has limited capa
 city\, please RSVP through the Eventbrite link below: https://www.eventbri
 te.ca/e/illu-150-celebration-opening-reception-website-launch-fundraiser-t
 ickets-2002562868447 Event organizer & contact: Associate Professor & Illu
 stration Program Chair | OCADU Faculty of Design Shea Chang schang@ocadu.c
 a\n\nImage credits: A MILLI-PICTURE IS WORTH A WORD\, Paul Dallas\, 2026. 
 ILLU150 Logo design by Gary Taxali\, 2026
LOCATION:Ada Slaight Student Gallery 100 McCaul St. 2nd floor MCA 225 + 22
 8
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/illu-150-celebration-opening-reception-web
 site-launch-fundraiser-tickets-2002562868447
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:now and then Artist/Curator Talk: Michael Massie in Conversation w
 ith Alysa Procida
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T183000
UID:curator-talk-michael-massie-conversation-alysa-procida@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Don't miss this exclusive Artist/Curator Talk with acclaimed a
 rtist Michael Massie and guest curator Alysa Procida.\n\nnow and then Arti
 st/Curator Talk: Michael Massie in Conversation with Alysa Procida Wednesd
 ay\, October 28\, 5 p.m. to 6:30 p.m. Don't miss this exclusive Artist/Cur
 ator Talk with acclaimed artist Michael Massie and guest curator Alysa Pro
 cida . Discover the stories exhibited in now and then \, celebrating Massi
 e's remarkable career through an extraordinary collection of teapots\, pre
 viously unexhibited and new works. Together\, they will explore the joy\, 
 humour\, and experimentation that define Massie's practice\, and discuss h
 ow his exceptional craftsmanship weaves together Inuit design traditions\,
  community\, and political commentary while continually challenging expect
 ations of contemporary Inuit art. Visit Registration Page About the Artist
  Michael Massie was born in Happy Valley-Goose Bay and currently resides i
 n Kippens\, NL. His artwork reflects his mixed Inuit and Scottish heritage
 \, such as his iconic ulu teapot works. He has been working in sculpture\,
  painting\, and drawing for over thirty years and has achieved artistic ac
 claim in Canada and internationally. His work sits in collections includin
 g the Smithsonian National Museum of the American Indian\, Heard Museum\, 
 Royal Ontario Museum\, National Gallery of Canada\, The Rooms\, Winnipeg A
 rt Gallery\, Montreal Museum of Fine Art\, and the YVR Vancouver Airport C
 ollection. He has been shortlisted twice for the Prix Saidye-Bronfman\, an
  honorary distinction for a Canadian craftsperson who demonstrates excelle
 nce in fine crafts. He was elected a member of the Royal Canadian Academy 
 of Arts in 2011 and inducted into the Order of Canada in 2017. Massie rece
 ived an honorary doctorate from OCAD University in 2024. About the Guest C
 urator Alysa Procida is an arts administrator\, curator\, and consultant w
 ho is passionate about connecting artists with audiences across the world.
  She is the 2026 International Liaison for the Arctic Arts Summit Secretar
 iat\, having previously co-organized the 2022 Arctic Arts Summit in Whiteh
 orse\, YK. Previously\, she was the Executive Director of the Inuit Art Fo
 undation (IAF) and Publisher of the Inuit Art Quarterly (IAQ)\, Chair of t
 he Magazines Canada Board of Directors\, and a mentor on the Inuit Futures
  in Arts Leadership: The Pilimmaksarniq / Pijariuqsarniq Project. As Publi
 sher of the IAQ \, Alysa oversaw a full redesign of the magazine in conjun
 ction with the IAF’s 30th anniversary in 2017 and the magazine’s first
  National Magazine Award in 2018. In 2019\, she was shortlisted for Publis
 her Grand Prix at the National Magazine Awards\, and in 2021 the IAQ was a
 warded Best Arts and Literary Magazine and winner of the Magazine Grand Pr
 ix. Onsite Gallery is generously supported by The Delaney Family We also a
 cknowledge the support of Ontario Arts Council\, an agency of the Ontario 
 Government and City of Toronto through Toronto Arts Council.
LOCATION:Onsite Gallery (RHD) 199 Richmond Street West 199 Richmond Street
  West
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/now-and-then-artist/curato
 r-talk-michael-massie-conversation-alysa-procida
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OCAD U x Tonkin Liu - Design Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T200000
UID:ocad-u-x-tonkin-liu-design-talk@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join Tonkin Liu\, the award-winning studio working across arch
 itecture\, art\, and landscape\, for a special talk exploring the creative
  possibilities of learning from nature.\n\nOCAD U x Tonkin Liu - Design Ta
 lk Date/Time: Tuesday\, October 27\, 2026\, 6:00 - 8:00 p.m. Location: RBC
  Centre for Emerging Artists & Designers (CEAD)\, 115 McCaul St.\, Level 3
  RSVP to attend Join Tonkin Liu \, the award-winning studio working across
  architecture\, art\, and landscape\, for a special talk exploring the cre
 ative possibilities of learning from nature. Their global practice brings 
 storytelling and technical invention together to create places that engage
  the senses and respond to their surroundings. Their new book\, Asking\, L
 ooking\, Playing\, Making: A Nature-Focused Design Process \, opens up thi
 s approach\, revealing how curiosity and experimentation turn initial idea
 s into buildings rooted in place.
LOCATION:Rosalie Sharp Pavillion (MCD) 115 McCaul St. Level 3
URL:https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/H8eiaeBjAQ
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Week!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T235959
UID:wellness-week@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Free food\, raffles/prizes\, workshops and more!\n\nA 3-day Ev
 ent: October 27-29\n\nFollow us on Instagram to keep up with updates!\n\nT
 he Student Wellness Centre will be hosting a 3-day wellness event this yea
 r. There will be food\, activities\, prizes and an opportunity to learn ab
 out the different resources available to OCAD U students.\n\nCheck out wha
 t we will be offering each day below. We hope to see you there!\n\nWellnes
 s Tabling Event October 27th 11 a.m. to 4 p.m. 100 McCaul St.\, Main Lobby
  We will be hosting a tabling event providing students with academic\, men
 tal/physical health resources! There will be free hot lunch\, activities a
 nd a chance to enter our raffle for giveaways such as gift cards and Saje 
 wellness bundles. Who you can expect! Student Wellbeing Centre for Learnin
 g & Teaching International Student's Office Alumo Good2Talk Campus Life We
 st Toronto Ontario Health Team\n\nHarm Reduction Workshop October 28th 12 
 p.m. 230 Richmond St W.\, Student Living Room (8F) The SWC within OCAD U h
 as partnered with local community health centres\, other colleges and univ
 ersities to begin connecting with students about Harm Reduction. Come join
  us for a free pizza lunch and meet some of our partners who are doing ama
 zing Harm Reduction work in Toronto. The workshop will allow for students 
 to learn and ask questions about Harm Reduction (ie: safer drug use practi
 ces\, the toxic toronto drug supply\, nalaxone\, drug prohibition/mass inc
 arceration\, HIV and Hep C) and to provide input on how the wellness centr
 e can implement this program effectively. Workshop led by Chance Cordon\, 
 Manager\, Harm Reduction Project.\n\nDecompression Day October 29th 10 a.m
 . to 6 p.m. 230 Richmond St W.\, Student Living Room (8F) As important as 
 it is to be proactive with your wellness\, sometimes its about decompressi
 ng and winding down. Come by the Student Living Room to enjoy a relaxing a
 ctivity day. There will be paint-your-own mugs (while supplies last)\, sna
 cks and vibey music.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street & Student Living Room
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/wellness-week
