BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Conversation | Rebecca Baird and Kenny Baird with Lisa Deanne S
 mith and Dr. Lilian Radovac
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T150000
UID:conversation-rebecca-baird-and-kenny-baird-lisa-deanne-smith-and-dr-li
 lian@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging conversation and exhibition tour with 
 artists Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird\, alongside exhibition curator
  Lisa Deanne Smith and scholar Dr. Lilian Radovac\, as they explore the st
 ories\, creative processes\, and lived experiences behind Returning to Our
 selves.\n\nIn Conversation | Rebecca Baird and Kenny Baird with Lisa Deann
 e Smith and Dr. Lilian Radovac – Saturday\, October 24\, 2026\, 1:00 p.m
 . to 3:00 p.m.\, Onsite Gallery\, 199 Richmond Street West\, Toronto Join 
 us for an engaging conversation and exhibition tour with artists Rebecca B
 aird and Kenny Alvin Baird \, alongside exhibition curator Lisa Deanne Smi
 th and scholar Dr. Lilian Radovac \, as they explore the stories\, creativ
 e processes\, and lived experiences behind Returning to Ourselves. Spannin
 g more than four decades of artistic practice\, Returning to Ourselves sho
 wcases the transformative work of Rebecca and Kenny Alvin Baird through sc
 ulpture\, painting\, traditional material practices\, interior design\, fi
 lm art direction\, graphic design\, and public art commissions. Together\,
  the artists and curator will reflect on the exhibition's themes of identi
 ty\, family\, creativity\, and Cree Métis cultural continuity\, offering 
 unique insights into the evolution of their multidisciplinary practices an
 d the enduring impact of their work. Visit Registration Page Image banner 
 credit: Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird \, 1991. Image courtesy of the
  artists.
LOCATION:Onsite Gallery (RHD) 199 Richmond Street West 199 Richmond Street
  West
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/conversation-rebecca-baird
 -and-kenny-baird-lisa-deanne-smith-and-dr-lilian
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Creates Change Richard Fung
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T190057
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T210057
UID:art-creates-change-richard-fung@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:OCAD University’s Faculty of Art presents: ART CREATES CHANG
 E The Kim Pruesse Speakers Series\n\nThe Kim Pruesse Speakers Series Richa
 rd Fung Artist Talk & Reception: Thursday\, October 22\, 7 pm OCAD Univers
 ity Auditorium 100 McCaul St.\, M5T 1W1\, Level 1\, Room 190 Free to the p
 ublic Wheelchair accessible\n\nAbout Richard Fung Richard Fung’s broad r
 ange of work\, from his acclaimed videos to his critical writing\, provide
  an analytical compass and a justice orientation\, drawing on the many int
 ersections of his own life: family histories and personal narratives\, Asi
 an masculinities\, queer continuities\, and Trinidadian/Caribbean history 
 and culture. In examining these representations and formations he highligh
 ts policing\, immigration\, racism and homophobia within the larger contex
 t of colonialism’s impositions. As an activist Fung was cofounder of Gay
  Asians of Toronto (GAT) and in the arts\, cofounder of the Images Festiva
 l. He is the recipient of a Rockefeller fellowship\, the Bell Canada Award
  for video art\, the Toronto Arts Award for media arts\, and the Kessler A
 ward from CLAGS: Center for LGBTQ Studies at the City University of New Yo
 rk\, among other recognitions. Richard is Professor Emeritus in the Facult
 y of Art.\n\nSea in the Blood Islands\n\nMy Mothers Funny Enigma Dog\n\nAr
 t Creates Change is a long-running lecture series\, now in its 20th year\,
  sponsored by the Faculty of Art at OCAD University. The series focuses on
  artists whose work engages and challenges the conventions of creative pra
 ctice and political imperatives\, and their various locations of agency. E
 vents are often co-sponsored with programs and organizations both within a
 nd beyond the university. This year\, in recognition of OCAD University’
 s 150th anniversary\, we are focusing on three faculty members: Bonnie Dev
 ine\, Richard Fung and Lillian Allen\, three artists whose work has helped
  shape not only OCAD\, but also the larger culture and political conversat
 ions of our time. Their creative\, academic and political work organically
  engages urgent public conversations about representation\, justice\, equi
 ty and relational power\, and embodies OCAD’s vision of “a vibrant com
 munity of bold\, curious and compassionate artists\, designers and scholar
 s imagining a creative\, joyful\, equitable and sustainable world.” Even
 ts are often co-sponsored with programs and organizations both within and 
 beyond the university. Each event includes an artist presentation\, Q&A\, 
 and a following reception. The events are free and open to the public and 
 university communities.\n\nThe Art Creates Change 2026 is supported by Mar
 k S Bonham Centre for Sexual Diversity Studies at UT OCAD U Art & Social C
 hange INTM: LIFE STUDIES SPECIALIZATION in the Faculty of Art through a ge
 nerous donation of the Joan and Clifford Hatch Foundation. Follow OCAD U F
 aculty of Art on Social Media 2026 Co-programmers: b.h. Yael & Min Sook Le
 e
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street Auditorium\, MCA190
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/art-creates-change-richard
 -fung
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
